    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/senior-change-communications-adviser-621547.html": {
      "title": "Senior Change Communications Adviser (4993)",
      "description": "Senior Change Communications Adviser (4993) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Senior Change Communications Adviser Faculty/Directorate Academic Services School/Function Corporate Affairs Contract type Fixed Term Contract Location of vacancy Penrhyn Road Actual hours 37 Salary from 45,925.00 Salary to 49,796.00 Posted Date 15/10/2026 Closing Date 23/10/2026 Ref No 4993 Documents Candidate Pack (PDF , 10784.32kb) Job Description (PDF , 198.8kb) The Role This is an exciting opportunity to play a central role in a major strategic project, shaping communications that inform, engage and support colleagues across the University. Working on a transformation initiative with institution-wide reach, you will develop and deliver clear, compelling and timely messaging, ensuring colleagues understand key developments and their wider context. We're looking for an exceptional writer who can bring clarity to complexity. Working closely with the project team, Human Resources colleagues and senior leaders, you will create high-quality content that informs, engages and builds understanding. From leadership briefings and staff updates to FAQs, intranet content and key messages, you will produce polished, audience-focused communications that are clear, concise and impactful, while handling sensitive issues with judgement, professionalism and discretion. This is a hands-on role for an outstanding communicator who thrives on producing impactful content. Taking a proactive approach, you will ensure communications build understanding, maintain confidence and help colleagues to stay informed, understand what matters most and feel connected to the University's priorities and future direction. The Person You are an exceptional communicator with outstanding writing, editing and proofreading skills, and a talent for turning complex information into clear, accessible and compelling content. With a strong eye for detail, you produce high-quality communications at pace while maintaining accuracy and consistency. You bring experience of supporting communications for complex programmes, projects or transformation initiatives, alongside a strong understanding of how to reach different audiences through a range of communications channels. You are comfortable balancing competing priorities, working to tight deadlines and adapting your approach to meet evolving requirements. A proactive, solutions-focused professional, you are skilled at providing trusted advice, influencing stakeholders and developing communications approaches that support organisational objectives. Directorate/Function The Corporate Affairs function sits within the Academic Services Directorate and plays a pivotal role in shaping and amplifying Kingston University’s story. Leading communications, public affairs, stakeholder engagement and reputation-building activity, the function strengthens the University’s profile, extends its influence and showcases the impact of its teaching, research and knowledge exchange. It plays a central role in positioning the University as a distinctive, authoritative and credible voice across higher education, industry, government and in civic life. The Academic Services Directorate includes Research & Impact, Knowledge Exchange, Academic Registry, Quality Assurance and Enhancement, the Learning and Teaching Enhancement Centre, Corporate Affairs and Development, Alumni Relations & Engagement (DARE). Collectively the Directorate supports academics in their research and KE activities and supports some of the University’s governance and decision-making committees, maintains academic regulations, develops and implements academic policies, oversees the quality and standards of academic provision and leads the development of education practices across the University. The Directorate is responsible for stimulating cutting edge research, impact and knowledge exchange and supporting a vibrant community of graduate research students, to increase the volume, impact and visibility of our research and business activities. We actively liaise with Faculties and researchers to support and develop research activities across all disciplines and provide related training and development opportunities. We foster interdisciplinary working to promote, advance and share knowledge with the overall aim of securing new revenue sources and contributing to regional prosperity. Our goal is to foster and sustain a vibrant research culture in which our researchers and research students can flourish. As a directorate, we identify opportunities for innovation, see change as an opportunity, value constructive feedback and share good practice across the University. Further information This is a full time, fixed term position for 12 months with a starting salary of £45,925 per annum, commensurate with experience. For informal enquiries, please contact Nicky Baird , Interim Director of Brand, Communications and Public Affairs. Please note this role is being managed by our agency and you should apply directly through the link below, quoting the reference number JN-102026-7125129. Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply Now Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Accept All Cookies Reject All Cookies Settings Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types