    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/research-fellow-nihr-london-arc-postdoctoral-researcher-620916.html": {
      "title": "Research Fellow",
      "description": "Research Fellow - NIHR London ARC Postdoctoral Researcher (4980) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Research Fellow - NIHR London ARC Postdoctoral Researcher Faculty/Directorate Faculty of Health, Science, Social Care & Education School/Function School of Nursing, Allied & Public Health Contract type Fixed Term Contract Location of vacancy Kingston Hill Actual hours 29.6 Salary from 45,925.00 Salary to 49,796.00 Posted Date 15/10/2026 Closing Date 08/11/2026 Ref No 4980 Documents Advert Details (PDF , 195kb) Candidate Pack (PDF , 10886.05kb) Job Description (PDF , 278.96kb) The NIHR Applied Research Collaboration (ARC) London is seeking to appoint a Postdoctoral Researcher to join the Research Inclusion team, led by Professor Tushna Vandrevala at Kingston University. The post is an NIHR Career Development Award, with a planned start date of 1 December 2026. NIHR ARCs bring together universities, NHS organisations, local authorities, health and care providers, voluntary and community organisations, and the public to deliver applied research that improves health and social care services and outcomes. The ARC London Research Inclusion theme aims to strengthen inclusive research practices, address structural barriers to participation and ensure research better reflects and benefits London's diverse and underserved communities. Based within Kingston University's School of Nursing, Allied and Public Health, you will play a leading role in delivering Research Inclusion initiatives across London. Working collaboratively with academic, NHS, local authority, VCSE and community partners, you will: Design, deliver and evaluate research inclusion projects involving underserved communities. Develop evidence-informed approaches, practical resources and guidance to embed inclusive research practices. Build partnerships and support training and capacity-building across the research community. Contribute to academic publications, knowledge mobilisation activities and future research funding proposals. Career development opportunities This NIHR Career Development Award offers an opportunity to develop your interdisciplinary research profile and progress towards research independence and leadership. Our ARC London Career Development Award holders will have regular networking opportunities and be members of the NIHR Academy ( benefits of academy membership ), with access to networking and professional development opportunities. These include a personalised development plan, peer mentorship, research leadership activities and opportunities to apply for training and development funding. You will also benefit from support in research inclusion, patient and public involvement and engagement (PPIE), implementation science and knowledge mobilisation. The Person You will normally hold a PhD in a relevant discipline or have submitted your thesis for examination by the time of application and expect it to be awarded before taking up the post. You will have a strong track record in applied health or social care research. You will have experience or a strong interest in research inclusion, health inequalities and working with underserved populations. We particularly welcome candidates with experience of co-production, PPIE, participatory research or community partnerships. You will be able to design and deliver high-quality research, collaborate across professional and community settings, and communicate findings effectively to academic and non-academic audiences. You will demonstrate strong research integrity, organisational and communication skills, and a commitment to making research more inclusive and accessible. This role would suit an ambitious researcher seeking to develop their research leadership while contributing to meaningful change in health and social care research. We welcome applications from researchers across a range of disciplinary backgrounds. The Faculty School of Nursing , Allied and Public Health Our people are passionate about developing nurses for the future, in each of the four fields of nursing – adult, children, learning disability and mental health. We support our students to ensure they get the skills and knowledge they need to make a lasting impact on society. We also have access to industry-leading research for nursing and health professions. Further information This is a part time (29.60 hours per week), fixed term position available until 31 March 2031 with a starting salary of £36,740 per annum (80% pro rata to £45,925 per annum). Interviews are expected to be held on Tuesday 17 November 2026 . For informal enquiries, please contact Professor Tushna Vandrevala . Applicants may also contact ARC London Research Capacity Development Lead, Professor Priscilla Harries to explore their suitability for these career development awards. Further information: Opportunities for NIHR Academy Members supported in our Infrastructure and Capacity Building Structures Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us"
    },
    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/lecturer-in-real-estate-621214.html": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Real Estate",
      "description": "Lecturer in Real Estate (4987) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Lecturer in Real Estate Faculty/Directorate Faculty of Business and Social Sciences School/Function Kingston Business School Contract type Permanent Location of vacancy Kingston Hill Actual hours 37 Salary from 45,925.00 Salary to 49,796.00 Posted Date 12/10/2026 Closing Date 13/11/2026 Ref No 4987 Documents Job Profile (PDF , 210.91kb) Kingston Business School is seeking to appoint an ambitious, talented and practice-focused Lecturer in Real Estate to join the growing Real Estate Team at the Kingston Business School and Department of Accounting, Finance and Informatics. The appointment will strengthen our Real Estate teaching capacity at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. We are particularly interested in candidates with professional or industry expertise in property and land law, landlord and tenant, property agency practice, planning and development, and/or real estate asset management. The successful candidate will contribute to high-quality teaching, assessment, marking, module leadership and student support across our Real Estate portfolio. You will bring current professional practice into the classroom and contribute to curriculum development, quality enhancement, professional accreditation, student recruitment and engagement within industry. This role is well suited to a real estate practitioner or academic with substantial industry experience. Professional standing, relevant sector experience and the ability to teach and assess applied Real Estate subjects are particularly important. The role also provides opportunities to contribute to research, scholarly activity and knowledge exchange aligned with Kingston University's Research Domain Framework. Depending on your professional and academic profile, this may include applied research, publications, conference activity, industry collaboration and engagement with external partners. The Person You will have a relevant postgraduate qualification in Real Estate, Surveying, Property/Land Law, Planning or a closely related discipline, together with substantial relevant professional or industry experience. You should be able to teach and assess at undergraduate and postgraduate level in at least two of the following areas: property/land law; landlord and tenant law and practice; property agency law and practice; planning and development; and real estate asset/property management. Chartered Surveyor status (MRICS/FRICS) or another relevant professional qualification would be highly desirable. A PhD or professional doctorate in a relevant discipline is desirable but not essential. Strong professional expertise and practice-based knowledge are particularly valued You will be an effective communicator who can translate legislation, case law, professional standards and complex real estate practice into engaging learning for diverse student cohorts. Experience of module leadership, curriculum development and professional accreditation would be advantageous. The Faculty The Department of Accounting, Finance and Informatics is a vibrant and growing academic community within Kingston Business School. The Department delivers a broad portfolio of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes and maintains strong links with industry, professional bodies and external stakeholders. Our academic staff are actively engaged in research, knowledge exchange and pedagogic innovation, creating an environment that supports both academic excellence and professional relevance. The successful candidate will join a collegial and supportive department committed to delivering an outstanding student experience and fostering impactful research. Directorate/Function Kingston Business School is recognised for its commitment to excellent education, impactful research and strong engagement with industry and the professions. The School promotes an inclusive, innovative, ambitious and enterprising culture, aligned with Kingston University's values and Town House Strategy. We welcome applications from candidates who will contribute to the diversity and strength of our academic community and who share our commitment to creating an inclusive environment where students and staff can thrive. Further information This is a full-time, permanent position with a starting salary of £45,925.00 per annum. Interviews are due to be in person on Wednesday 9 December 2026. For informal enquiries, please contact Dr John Sebastian Pereira , Head of Department, Accounting, Finance and Informatics. Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us"
    },
    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/hpl-dept-of-accounting-finance-informatics-621215.html": {
      "title": "HPL",
      "description": "HPL - Dept of Accounting, Finance & Informatics (4988) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions HPL - Dept of Accounting, Finance & Informatics Faculty/Directorate Faculty of Business and Social Sciences School/Function Kingston Business School Contract type Fixed Term Contract Location of vacancy Kingston Hill Actual hours 0 Posted Date 12/10/2026 Closing Date 13/11/2026 Ref No 4988 Documents Job Profile (PDF , 158.27kb) The Role Kingston Business School is seeking an enthusiastic and committed Hourly Paid Lecturer to join our student-focused academic community within the Department of Accounting, Finance and Informatics. To provide flexible teaching, assessment and marking support across undergraduate and postgraduate Real Estate provision. The role is intended to provide additional practice-based capacity, particularly in legal, regulatory and professional areas of Real Estate. Priority teaching areas - Property and land law, including legal interests, tenure, covenants, easements and land registration. - Landlord and tenant law and practice, including commercial leases, lease renewal, rent review, notices, tenant default and dispute resolution. - Property agency law and practice, including estate agency regulation, lettings, sales, consumer protection, AML, professional standards and conveyancing processes. - Planning, land use and development, including planning law and policy, development control, development agreements, viability and development appraisal. - Real estate asset/property management, including lease events, asset strategy, occupier/investor requirements, performance and professional practice. The Person · - Relevant postgraduate qualification or equivalent professional standing in Real Estate, Surveying, Property/Land Law, Planning, the Built Environment or a closely related field. · - Substantial current or recent professional/industry experience in real estate/property practice. · - Ability to teach, assess and mark at undergraduate and/or postgraduate level in at least two of the priority teaching areas. · - Ability to apply current legislation, case law, regulation and professional standards to teaching and assessment. · - Strong communication skills and ability to support diverse student cohorts. · - Availability to contribute flexibly to teaching and marking requirements. Desirable · - MRICS/FRICS or another relevant professional qualification. · - Previous higher education teaching and/or marking experience. · - FHEA or equivalent teaching recognition. - Experience of professional accreditation or RICS-aligned curriculum. - Priority teaching areas · - Property and land law, including legal interests, tenure, covenants, easements and land registration. · - Landlord and tenant law and practice, including commercial leases, lease renewal, rent review, notices, tenant default and dispute resolution. · - Property agency law and practice, including estate agency regulation, lettings, sales, consumer protection, AML, professional standards and conveyancing processes. · - Planning, land use and development, including planning law and policy, development control, development agreements, viability and development appraisal. · - Real estate asset/property management, including lease events, asset strategy, occupier/investor requirements, performance and professional practice. The Faculty At Kingston Business School, we value colleagues who are committed to innovation, inclusivity, and supporting students to achieve their full potential. If you are looking for an opportunity to contribute to a vibrant and professionally engaged learning environment, we would love to hear from you. Directorate/Function Kingston Business School has triple accreditation, which recognises the high quality and standard of our business degree offering. The AACSB (Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business) Business Accreditation signals to the world that Kingston Business School has met the most rigorous standards of excellence in business education.  In addition, many of our courses are also accredited and recognised by professional bodies, including the Chartered Institute of Marketing, the Chartered Institute of Personnel and Development, the Association of Corporate Treasurers, and the Royal Institution of Chartered Surveyors (RICS). Further information Standard Kingston rates of pay apply and currently start at: £23.80 (including London Weighting, not including holiday pay) for both teaching and non-teaching hours. One lecturing hour includes preparation, delivery, follow up and related administration and attracts a multiplier of 2.25 increasing the hourly rate to £53.55. Non-teaching hours include tutorials, meetings, induction and invigilation. Interviews will be held on w/c 23rd November 2026 For informal enquiries, please contact Dr John Sebastian Pereira , Head of Department: Accounting, Finance, and Informatics (DAFI). Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Accept All Cookies Reject All Cookies Settings Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices"
