    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/senior-hr-advisor-621731.html": {
      "title": "Senior HR Advisor (5000)",
      "description": "Senior HR Advisor  (5000) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Senior HR Advisor Faculty/Directorate Human Resources School/Function HR Advice & Reward Contract type Permanent Location of vacancy Penrhyn Road Actual hours 37 Posted Date 19/10/2026 Closing Date 09/11/2026 Ref No 5000 Documents Candidate Pack (PDF , 10784.32kb) Job Description (PDF , 201.98kb) The Role This is an exciting opportunity to join Kingston University's HR Advice & Reward team as a Senior HR Advisor, contributing to the University's people agenda through expert HR advice, policy development and the delivery of strategic HR projects. You will provide pragmatic, solutions-focused advice to managers and senior leaders on complex people matters, using your employment law expertise and professional judgement to balance organisational risk, employee experience and business objectives. You will lead and contribute to strategic HR projects and organisational change initiatives, driving improvements to HR services, workforce practices and employee experience. You will also take ownership of HR policy development and review, ensuring policies remain legally compliant, reflect best practice and support an inclusive, high-performing culture. You will lead on complex employee relations matters, including disciplinary, grievance, capability, performance and sickness absence cases, as well as supporting ACAS Early Conciliation and Employment Tribunal processes. Using HR data and insights, you will identify trends, address underlying issues and develop proactive solutions that improve organisational effectiveness. Working collaboratively with stakeholders across faculties and professional services, you will strengthen management capability, influence decision-making and support the continuous improvement of HR services. As a senior member of the team, you will also provide guidance to HR colleagues and act as an escalation point for complex issues. The Person You will be an experienced HR professional with a strong track record of advising on complex employee relations and employment law matters, alongside experience of leading HR projects, developing or reviewing policies and supporting organisational change. You will have excellent employment law and HR knowledge, supported by a relevant CIPD, employment law or equivalent qualification, and the ability to translate legislation and organisational requirements into practical, effective solutions. You will be confident influencing senior stakeholders, managing competing priorities and using HR data to identify trends, evaluate initiatives and inform evidence-based decisions. Excellent communication, analytical and relationship-building skills are essential, alongside a proactive, customer-focused approach, sound judgement and a commitment to equality, diversity and inclusion. You will also demonstrate the ability to support and develop colleagues, remain resilient when managing challenging situations and drive continuous improvement. Higher Education experience is welcomed, but relevant experience in other large or complex organisations will also be considered. Directorate/Function The Human Resources Directorate provides the people strategy, expertise and infrastructure that enables Kingston University to achieve its ambitions. You will join our experienced HR Advice & Reward team, working alongside HR colleagues across the University to provide both responsive operational support and proactive, strategic people advice. We work in partnership with academic faculties and professional services to help managers get the best from their people, tackle challenges effectively and create an environment in which our staff can perform, develop and contribute to the University's success. As a Senior HR Advisor, you will play an important role in developing this partnership, helping us move beyond simply responding to individual HR issues towards earlier intervention, stronger management capability and continuous improvement in our HR service. Further information This is a full-time, permanent Grade 9 position, salary up to £60,492. The HR team is based at our Penrhyn Road campus, with colleagues required to travel across the University's campuses according to business needs. Please include a copy of your CV with your application and tell us how your skills, knowledge and experience will enable you to be successful in this role. For informal enquiries about the position, please contact Jo Willoughby, Head of HR Advice & Reward. J.Willoughby@kingston.ac.uk Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Accept All Cookies Reject All Cookies Settings Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices"
