    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/graduate-scheme-2026-27-621693.html": {
      "title": "Graduate Scheme 2026/27 (4997)",
      "description": "Graduate Scheme 2026/27 (4997) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Graduate Scheme 2026/27 Faculty/Directorate Students School/Function Students Contract type Permanent Location of vacancy Penrhyn Road Actual hours 37 Posted Date 19/10/2026 Closing Date 09/11/2026 Ref No 4997 Documents Candidate Pack (PDF , 3522.64kb) CSA Administrator JD (PDF , 225.93kb) Information Centre Asssistant JD (PDF , 191.65kb) Practice Placement Administrator- JD (PDF , 297.54kb) Student Engagement Administrator- JD (PDF , 123.1kb) The Role This isn't your typical graduate role. It's a permanent opportunity to launch your career in Higher Education. As part of our Graduate intake, you'll join a team within the Directorate for Students, helping to deliver services, projects and initiatives that enhance the student experience and support student success. No two days are the same. Depending on your role, you could be supporting students with enquiries, coordinating projects, analysing data and insights, using system management tools, developing communications using multiple channels, improving services and processes, engaging directly with students, or collaborating with colleagues across the University to bring new ideas to life. Working alongside experienced professionals, you'll take on real responsibility, build your confidence, and develop skills in data management, data system management, customer service, stakeholder engagement, communication, problem-solving and service delivery. Whether you are looking to build a long-term career in Higher Education or gain transferable skills that open doors across a range of sectors, these roles provide an excellent foundation for your future. For the details of roles available, please refer to the full job details. As part of the application, you will order the advertised roles according to your preference. The Person We're looking for ambitious graduates who are ready to learn, grow and make an impact. You'll bring energy, curiosity and a commitment to delivering an excellent experience for students and colleagues. A confident communicator and collaborative team player, you'll enjoy building relationships, solving problems and taking ownership of your work. You'll thrive in a fast-paced environment, have a keen eye for detail, ability to work with large data sets, adapt to new challenges and be keen to develop your skills through feedback and experience. Most importantly, you'll share Kingston University's values of being Enterprising, Innovative, Inclusive and Ambitious, and be excited by the opportunity to help shape the student experience. Directorate/Function The Students’ Directorate key aim within the Townhouse strategy is to deliver a seamless, high-quality experience for all current and future students to ensure they are “sought after”, supporting their participation, achievements and success before, during and after their time at Kingston. Further information These graduate roles are all full time, permanent positions with a starting salary of £30,067 per annum. Eligibility Recruitment for the 2026/2027 cohort is open to all graduates who have achieved a degree in any subject in the past two years (between May 2024 and August 2026). You do not need to be a graduate of Kingston University London. Under the current UK Immigration Rules, roles on the Graduate Scheme do not meet eligibility requirements for sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa.  This means the University would not be able to sponsor candidates for the Graduate Scheme for a Skilled Worker visa.  So if you require immigration permission to work in the UK, you would need permission in an alternative immigration route that permits working in a role on the Graduate Scheme.  Graduate Route visa holders would have the necessary immigration permission to work in Graduate Scheme roles, but the University would not be able to sponsor you for a Skilled Worker visa on the expiry of your Graduate Route visa. The Assessment Process Stage 1 : Submit your application form by 9 November 2026 . Please refer carefully to the skills and competencies required. We would encourage you to use examples from your studies, hobbies, travel, personal life, or work opportunities, or from any other relevant areas. As part of your application, please order the advertised roles according to your preference. Stage 2: If you are successful at the application stage, you will be invited to an assessment day on Tuesday 24 November 2026 where you'll take part in a variety of assessed activities. Stage 3 : If successful at assessment centre, you will be invited to attend an in-person individual interview with a hiring panel. For queries about the specific roles , please contact each individual job lead: -       Practice Placement Administrator role - Sally Long s.long@kingston.ac.uk -       CSA Administrator role – Steve Cameron s.cameron@kingston.ac.uk -       Information Centre Assistant role – Paolo Zanelli p.zanelli@kingston.ac.uk -       Student Engagement Administrator – Jane Hargreaves j.hargreaves@kingston.ac.uk For queries ab out the application process , please contact HR Shared Services KU-HR-JOBS@kingston.ac.uk Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Accept All Cookies Reject All Cookies Settings Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices"
