    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/research-associate-621734.html": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Research Associate (5001) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Research Associate Faculty/Directorate Faculty of Health, Science, Social Care & Education School/Function School of Nursing, Allied & Public Health Contract type Fixed Term Contract Location of vacancy Kingston Hill Actual hours 37 Salary from 40,195.00 Salary to 44,711.00 Posted Date 20/10/2026 Closing Date 15/11/2026 Ref No 5001 Documents Advert Details (PDF , 90.7kb) Candidate Pack (PDF , 10886.05kb) Job Description (PDF , 270.33kb) Are you passionate about tackling health inequalities through community-engaged research? Kingston University is seeking a Research Associate for CHAMPIONS-PT, an NIHR-funded programme co-designing and piloting a Community Champions intervention to improve routine vaccination uptake among Black African and Caribbean pregnant women and young children in London. Working with NHS and public health partners, local authorities, community organisations and people with lived experience, CHAMPIONS-PT will explore barriers to vaccination, develop culturally appropriate approaches and assess the feasibility and acceptability of the intervention. Based in the School of Nursing, Allied and Public Health and working with Professor Tushna Vandrevala, you will: -Support community engagement, lived-experience groups, co-design workshops and designathons. -Undertake qualitative data collection and analysis. -Support recruitment, study coordination and implementation and process evaluation of the pilot. -Contribute to publications, reports, presentations and knowledge mobilisation. This post offers an opportunity to develop expertise in participatory public health research, intervention development and health inequalities. Please note, an enhanced Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check clearance is required for the role. The Person You will normally be completing or have recently completed a PhD in social science, public health or a related discipline. You will bring qualitative research skills, experience of participatory or community-engaged approaches, and a commitment to inclusive research. Experience working with ethnically diverse communities or in maternal and child health would be valuable. You will be organised, collaborative and able to communicate effectively with academic, professional and community audiences. Please see attached Advert Details for more information. The Faculty School of Nursing , Allied and Public Health Our people are passionate about developing nurses for the future, in each of the four fields of nursing – adult, children, learning disability and mental health. We support our students to ensure they get the skills and knowledge they need to make a lasting impact on society. We also have access to industry-leading research for nursing and health professions. Further information This is a full time, fixed term position available for 2 years with a starting salary of £40,195 per annum; planned start date of 1 December 2026. Interviews are expected to be held on Wednesday 25 November 2026 . For informal enquiries, please contact Professor Tushna Vandrevala . Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us"
