    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/widening-access-and-outreach-manager-621744.html": {
      "title": "Widening Access and Outreach Manager (5002)",
      "description": "Widening Access and Outreach Manager (5002) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Widening Access and Outreach Manager Faculty/Directorate Students School/Function Student Recruitment & Admissions Contract type Permanent Location of vacancy Kingston Hill Actual hours 37 Salary from 51,163.00 Salary to 60,492.00 Posted Date 20/10/2026 Closing Date 22/11/2026 Ref No 5002 Documents Candidate Pack Professional Services (PDF , 10784.32kb) Students - 8003261 - Grade 9 - Widening Access and Outreach Manager - Oct26 - Job_Ref_5002 (PDF , 233.28kb) The Role We are seeking an experienced and strategic leader for the role of Widening Access and Outreach Manager at Kingston University. Working collaboratively with colleagues across the University and external partners, you will lead the development, delivery and evaluation of evidence-informed outreach activity that supports underrepresented learners to access and progress to higher education. You will lead and inspire the Widening Access and Outreach team, oversee delivery of Access interventions in the Access and Participation Plan and Schools and Colleges Strategy, and use data, evidence and evaluation to drive impact and continuous improvement. The role involves developing strategic partnerships with schools, colleges, community organisations and sector stakeholders, while working closely with faculties, student recruitment and admissions colleagues to ensure a coordinated approach that supports institutional priorities and delivers meaningful outcomes for learners. The Person Educated to degree level, or possessing equivalent relevant professional experience, you will have significant experience in widening access, outreach and strategic partnership development within higher education or a related education setting. You will possess a strong understanding of Access and Participation Plans, Office for Students regulation, and the barriers facing underrepresented learners in accessing higher education. You will have excellent leadership, communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to build effective relationships across schools, colleges, community organisations and university departments. Confident using data, evidence and evaluation to inform decision-making, you will be highly organised and able to manage multiple priorities effectively. You will also bring experience of leading and developing teams, delivering projects to a high standard, and a genuine commitment to promoting equality of opportunity through higher education. Directorate/Function The Student Directorate The wider directorate’s key aim within the strategy is to deliver a seamless, high-quality experience for all current and future students to ensure they are “sought after”, supporting their participation, attainment, and success before, during and after their time at Kingston. This in turn will create a culture of high performance that is inclusive, innovative ambitious and enterprising. Student Recruitment and Admissions The team’s primary objective is to achieve agreed student recruitment targets and contribute to the whole University’s recruitment and admissions functions ensuring good ROI and a first-class student experience throughout the applicant journey. Further information This is a full time, permanent position with a starting salary of £51,163 per annum. Interviews are expected to be held in the week commencing 07 December 2026. For informal enquiries, please contact Sukh Chonk – Student Recruitment and Admissions Director. Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Accept All Cookies Reject All Cookies Settings Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices"
    },
    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/information-centre-coordinator-621409.html": {
      "title": "Information Centre Coordinator",
      "description": "Information Centre Coordinator (4991) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Information Centre Coordinator Faculty/Directorate Students School/Function Student Services Contract type Permanent Location of vacancy Kingston Hill Actual hours 18.5 Posted Date 19/10/2026 Closing Date 01/11/2026 Ref No 4991 Documents Candidate Pack Professional Services (PDF , 10784.32kb) Students - 8009737_8009736- Grade 6 - Information Centre Coordinator - Oct26 - Job_Ref_4991 (PDF , 236.38kb) As part of the Information Centre team, this Information Centre Coordinator role supports the Information Centre Leadership team to develop and deliver high quality, innovative student-focused first-line Information Centre support services and oversight of library buildings. The role provides day-to-day supervision of Information Centre services, service points and staff workloads.   This is carried out via help desks and staff offices, in person, by phone and using enquiry management systems. The Information Centre acts as the first point of contact for a variety of student support services across the University, answering with empathy a wide range of student enquiries. The Information Centre Coordinator role also acts as a point of referral for more complex, multi-faceted enquiries taking a proactive approach to supporting members of the team. The role provides support to students who require further generalist advice and guidance, navigating the University’s second line specialist advice services or accessing emergency support. The role is also expected to contribute to a positive team ethos and delivering agreed service and University objectives. The Information Centre Coordinator role is also responsible for the day-to-day supervision of library spaces including opening and closing building as required, managing behaviour and resolving and escalating issues within these spaces. This role is an on-campus position, that requires flexibility to work across all four sites as required including some evening and weekends depending on service requirements. The Person We are looking for someone who has the ability to proactively supervise and support Information Centre services and service points, direct and coordinate the work of others in a fast-paced customer focused environment. You will have the ability to support colleagues dealing with a large volume of enquiries on a variety of subjects through various channels of communication such as help desks, telephones and an enquiry management system. You must have the ability to communicate effectively for a range of audiences. You will be able to show a demonstrable commitment to customer service and continuous service improvement and be able to work as part of a team and contribute positively to the team effort. You will have a good understanding of ‘Student Hub’ type support services (including Information Centre and Library services) and experience of using and supporting colleagues use enquiry management systems. You will show evidence of being IT literate with the ability to develop in-depth end user expertise. You will also have an understanding of mental health ‘first aid’. Directorate/Function The Student Services section provides the University’s first and second line services for students. The Information Centre is the sections’ first line team that supports the following second line teams: Library and Learning Services, Course & Student Administration, Student Engagement and Student Life, Health and Wellbeing. Services are designed to be accessible and inclusive of all students, to ensure their enquiries are resolved quickly and support is available to enable them to fully engage with and succeed in their studies. Further information There are 2 Part time permanent positions (18.5 hrs per week) with a starting salary of £34,007 pro rata per annum. This role is an on-campus position (no home working), that requires flexibility to work on occasions across all four sites. The successful candidates will be regularly working the following fixed work patterns and sites. Position Site/ Day Mon Tues Weds Thurs Fri Sat Sun 1 (18.5hrs) Penrhyn Road Information Centre / Library 08:15-13:00 off 08:30-13:00 08:15-13:00 08:15-13:00 off off 2 (18.5hrs) Kingston Hill Information Centre / Library 08:15-13:00 off 08:30-13:00 08:15-13:00 08:15-13:00 off off Short listed applicants will be invited to an online first stage interview call (week commencing 9 November 2026) to determine who will be invited to a subsequent in-person interview which will take place on week commencing 16 November 2026. For informal enquiries, please email both Paolo Zanelli and Bruce Mitchell , Head of Information Centre Services and Information Centre Operations Manager. Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us"
    },
    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/hourly-paid-lecturer-ecology-621713.html": {
      "title": "Hourly Paid Lecturer",
      "description": "Hourly Paid Lecturer - Ecology (4999) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Hourly Paid Lecturer - Ecology Faculty/Directorate Faculty of Engineering, Computing & the Environment School/Function School of Built Environment & Geography Contract type Fixed Term Contract Location of vacancy Penrhyn Road Actual hours 5 Posted Date 19/10/2026 Closing Date 09/11/2026 Ref No 4999 Documents Role Profile (Word , 47.35kb) We are looking for an Hourly Paid Lecturer to provide support for teaching in Ecology and conservation. You can expect approximately five hours per week on average plus associated preparation time. All taught sessions to be delivered at our Penrhyn Road Campus and local field settings. The Person The successful candidate must have a Doctorate in a related field or an equivalent professional qualification and be able to teach Environmental Science. You will be able to demonstrate teaching competency in field and laboratory settings. You should also be able to contribute to teaching quantitative research methods and supervise undergraduate and post graduate students. It would be desirable to have a relevant level of UKPSF recognition and an accreditation from a relevant professional body. It would also be expected that you are developing your research portfolio with regard to income generation and/or publications. Experience of managing undergraduate modules and working in a multidisciplinary environment would be desirable. You must have excellent communication skills and team working experience and be able to independently project manage set tasks and commitments to fixed deadlines. The Faculty The successful candidate will be joining the Department of Geography, Geology and the Environment. We actively promote our University core values of ambition, innovation, inclusivity and entrepreneurship in all our teaching and research endeavours, aligning with the University goal to maintain an outstanding reputation. Our TEF triple-Gold standard courses have a proven track record for teaching excellence. The Department sits within the Faculty of Engineering, Computing and the Environment and here there are also many opportunities to collaborate with colleagues, e.g. climate resilience, the built environment and the integration of Artificial Intelligence. Further information Standard Kingston rates of pay apply and currently start at £23.80 per hour (including London Weighting, not including holiday pay) for both teaching and non-teaching hours. One lecturing hour includes preparation, delivery, follow up and related administration and attracts a multiplier of 2.25 increasing the hourly rate to £53.55. Non-teaching hours include tutorials, meetings, induction and invigilation. Hourly Paid Lecturers are not expected to exceed an average of eight hours per week, over the duration of their contract. This is a fractional appointment until 31 July 2027. For informal enquiries, please contact Dr Stuart Downward , Head of Department of Geography, Geology & the Environment. Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom of Information Wider Information Set Privacy Cookies Charitable status Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us"
